{"id": "EUVD-2026-90970", "enisaUuid": "a0905795-ae69-343e-9f5f-5fd8d7e4800d", "description": "A flaw was found in rubygem-katello. An SQL injection vulnerability exists in the Red Hat Satellite Katello Registry Proxy. The application fails to sanitize input parameters used in database queries within the RegistryProxiesController. The methods check_blob_push_org_label and get_matching_products_from_org take user-supplied labels directly from the request path and interpolate them into raw SQL fragments. This flaw is accessible to a user with only the create_personal_access_tokens permission, even if the user access is restricted, with no Organization or Location assigned.", "datePublished": "2026-10-01T17:14:50", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-07T06:12:09", "baseScore": 6.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N", "references": ["https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:74503", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:74504", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:74505", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:74506", "https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-56097", "https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2490543"], "aliases": ["GHSA-mmq3-mv36-wfm7", "CVE-2026-56097"], "assigner": "redhat", "epss": 0.28, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0713bf04-cf8e-3c70-9ee7-8942e49f7210", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Satellite 6.17 for RHEL 9", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0:4.16.0.20-1.el9sat"}, {"id": "3d36e8c1-e768-3e2c-be1e-38cf3e27aef9", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Satellite 6.18 for RHEL 9", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0:4.18.0.24-1.el9sat"}, {"id": "60f724df-56ed-3d64-af5c-48de510df1e5", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Satellite 6.19 for RHEL 9", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0:4.20.0.11-1.el9sat"}, {"id": "7100023f-d2e6-3451-98bf-ffdbba408606", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Satellite 6.16 for RHEL 9", "vendor": {"name":